nm-freebsd is a NetworkManager D-Bus compatibility service for FreeBSD.

It owns org.freedesktop.NetworkManager on the system bus and exposes the
subset of the NetworkManager API used by plasma-nm, the GNOME network panel
and an included XFCE panel plugin. Wi-Fi operations are carried out through
wpa_supplicant, using its D-Bus interface when available and its native
control socket otherwise. Wired links and interface events are observed
through FreeBSD netlink.

The daemon does not start any desktop UI: KDE and GNOME use their native
frontends, while XFCE users can add the NetworkManager FreeBSD panel plugin.
